  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICMPS 2025 Cafemin Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x201c;Path to reconstruction: Emotional health and a dignified future for migrants&#x201d; project in Mexico,  (CAFEMIN), aims to strengthen comprehensive psychosocial care for migrants in the CAFEMIN shelter, through specialized support from a psychologist, a psychotherapist, and a psychiatrist. Through clinical processes and a transversal approach centered on the &apos;life project,&apos; therapeutic support will be provided for the recovery of emotional well-being, the reconstruction of a sense of identity, autonomous decision-making, and dignified integration in Mexico. The acquisition of psychiatric medication, clothing and shoes for migrants, and bedding for their resting areas is also planned; these supplies are part of their process of self-care, dignity, and reaffirmation of identity.</narrative>
  </description>
